{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation complete locally, all three residuals:\n1. AC1 (reduce path): new structural block in tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py spies the SHARED seam (_confirm.emit/emit_text) and asserts, per verb, exactly ONE routed line and stdout == that line + newline (nothing printed outside the seam) — parametrized over create/link/transition, plus a no-op-path variant (link re-link, transition already-at-status). Proved it is a real guard by mutation: replacing confirm_created's emit_text with a bare print makes create fail with 'routed 0 lines through the shared seam'. The event reducer was deliberately NOT the spy target: rebar.reducer.reduce_ticket is re-exported by binding the function object at import time (rebar.reducer.__init__, rebar._native, rebar.__init__), so a call-count on the defining module would silently under-report. The 'no follow-up store read' half is instead proved by test_confirmation_formatters_need_no_store, which formats create/comment/tag-noop/transition lines with cwd in an empty tmp dir and REBAR_ROOT deleted — no store exists to read.\n2. AC2 (verb inventory): curated MUTATION_VERBS in scripts/gen_cli_reference.py (17 rows = _WRITES_FULL | _LIFECYCLE), each with noop flag + condition, rendered as a 'Verb inventory: no-op-capable vs always-writes' table in the generated docs/cli-reference.md. Drift-gated two ways: _check_mutation_verbs() makes render() raise when the key set != rebar._cli._CONFIRM_SCOPE (so the CI drift gate fails on an unclassified verb), and test_an_unclassified_verb_fails_the_generator asserts that behaviour directly by deleting a row.\n3. AC3 (old->new mapping): same curated rows carry old/new columns, rendered as the 'Confirmation-line record (pre-42cd70b889 -> today)' table. Old strings were read out of git (42cd70b889^), not paraphrased: notably transition printed 'UNBLOCKED: <ids|none>' on a CLOSE ONLY and was silent on every other target, which is why reopen (a delegation to transition closed->open) was silent before.\nNOTE ON THE DOC: docs/cli-reference.md is GENERATED; it was regenerated with 'python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py', not hand-edited. Gates: make lint PASS (complexity active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0), make typecheck PASS (572 files)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787187356353471001,"uuid":"3dcd187d-f3a2-47da-b1f5-5892d43f3fd1"}